  "summary": "Musician-and-instrument-led poster auditions with two optional questions, available original/adjusted samples, saved working expectations and context-dependent practice focus/effort. Combined V20 also carries the prior bank expansion and whole-game poster work.",
  "changes": [
    "Approved portrait leads each supported audition. Actual available audio precedes progressive questions; questions and local practice choices refresh in place without scroll resets. Written fallback and unsupported genre limits are explicit.",
    "Working-style and commitment answers, plus the actual musical request, persist through the original recruitment/formation save. Rapport is player-to-musician, separate from the existing musician-pair relationship model.",
    "Two practice choices: Starts & Stops / Listen & Respond, and Steady Pace / One More Take. Actual fatigue, room tension, rapport, traits and actual attendance change the outcome; the same effort can help a fresh group or strain a worn one.",
    "Only genuinely fulfilled plans and actual participating musicians receive agreed-evening credit. Saved member reactions explain what happened, with full detailed notes.",
    "Reading, playback, local selection and navigation remain free. Original invitation cost, rehearsal fee/day, atomic save/rollback, once-only finance and legacy behavior remain protected."
